      "0093: exactly four white pom-poms, with duplicated and clipped ones removed; wind comes from the same side; left crate shelters the mat and porch post obscures half the red flower.",
      "0094: one tail per squirrel; self-hugging and stored warmth precede daytime nap; head rests on pillow and body is under the blanket; empty open chestnut during direct reunion hug.",
      "0095: muddy ball progresses from bottom dirt to spread dirt, dirt rotated up, small remaining patch and clean return; basin edge establishes floating ball; cloth touches ball.",
      "0096: orange scarf transfers from child to stone after page four; fixed grass stays at the same height while the stone rises on the folded scarf; white ridge light precedes sunrise; stone has no limbs and a single stone remains on final windowsill."
